From c47c4a12e63c0da69149f883506e041fd56646a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:09:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Give the video layer the color depth of the video

The layer used the EGL config of the scene graph's context, 8 bits per
channel, so a 10, 12 or 16 bit video was cut to 8. Choose the config of
the layer by the depth of the video (the pixel format mpv outputs): the
deepest the display offers up to it, 10 bits, or half float for more.
The surface is made again when the depth changes, and mpv is told the
depth of the framebuffer so that it dithers to it.

Qt creates its context with the config of the window, and Mesa refuses
to make that context current on a surface of another config
(EGL_BAD_MATCH for every 10 bit config), which Qt has no way to
change. With EGL_KHR_no_config_context the layer therefore draws in a
context of its own, of the same kind of OpenGL, without a config, and
mpv's render context is made in it. Without the extension the layer
stays at the 8 bits of the scene graph's context, as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
